    description: "USS Arkansas (BM-7) was the lead ship of the Arkansas-class monitors, commissioned in 1902. She displaced about 3,225 tons, measured roughly 78 metres and made 12.5 knots. Her entire main battery was a single forward twin 305mm/40 turret, backed by 102mm/50 guns, 57mm six-pounders and 37mm one-pounder rapid-fire guns. Renamed Ozark in 1909 to free the name for a new battleship, she became a submarine tender in 1913 and was decommissioned in 1919.",
