    "description": "The E13A, Navy Type 0 Reconnaissance Seaplane, was a three-seat twin-float seaplane that entered Imperial Japanese Navy service in 1941 and was catapult-launched from battleships, cruisers and seaplane tenders for fleet reconnaissance, gunnery spotting, anti-submarine patrol and liaison. About 1,418 were built. Its maximum speed was about 376 km/h with a range of about 2,089 km, and the single central float with wingtip outriggers gave the type its distinctive profile. In game it is a scout, armed with one flexible 7.7mm Type 92 machine gun in the rear cockpit; the E13A1c's belly-mounted 20mm cannon and 250 kg bomb load are not configured and are not listed in the reference.",
