      {
        label: "Torpedo Bombers",
        value: "6× B5N2",
      },
    ],
    description: "Hōshō was the first ship completed as a purpose-built aircraft carrier. Her experimental layout helped the Imperial Japanese Navy develop carrier doctrine and aviation procedures during the interwar period. Obsolete for combat by the Pacific War, she mainly served as a training carrier and survived to repatriate Japanese personnel after the surrender.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
      {
        name: "Wikipedia — Hōshō",
        url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japanese%20aircraft%20carrier%20H%C5%8Dsh%C5%8D",
