    description: "Kentucky (BB-66) was the sixth Iowa-class battleship. Laid down in 1942, her construction stalled when her main machinery was diverted to landing craft, and she was never completed, being sold for scrap in 1958. This drawing shows a battlecarrier conversion of that hull: the forward turret is retained while the rest of the ship becomes a hangar, a flight deck, and two elevators. It is a fictional design in the same line as the wartime studies for converting Iowa-class hulls into carriers.",
