    description: "The Kyūshū J7W1 Shinden was a Japanese Navy single-seat interceptor designed around a canard, rear-mounted engine, and six-bladed pusher propeller. Intended to engage high-altitude B-29 bombers, it was armed with four forward-firing 30 mm Type 5 cannon. Only two prototypes were completed; the first flew on 3 August 1945 and the type never entered combat service. In game it can carry two four-round 100 mm Type 3 rocket-bomb mounts, for eight anti-aircraft rockets.",
