    ],
    description: "USS Kentucky (BB-6) was the second Kearsarge-class pre-dreadnought, commissioned in 1900 with an unusual two-storey turret arrangement: a twin 203mm/35 turret superposed on each twin 330mm/35 main turret, backed by eighteen 127mm/40 secondary guns. By 1915 her torpedo tubes had been removed and she carried no anti-aircraft armament. She served as a training ship in the First World War, was decommissioned in 1920 and scrapped in 1923.",
