    description: "HMS Duke of York was a King George V-class battleship commissioned in 1941. In December 1943 she used radar-directed fire to cripple Scharnhorst at the Battle of the North Cape. Her 1944-45 refit strengthened the anti-aircraft armament before she became flagship of the British Pacific Fleet and witnessed the Japanese surrender in Tokyo Bay.",
