    description: "Sevastopol is the Project 69 large cruiser design offered to the Soviet Union by the Italian firm Ansaldo in 1936: hull and machinery followed Italian practice while the armament was Soviet. She takes her name from the second ship of the Kronshtadt class. The proposal was never built and remained on paper.",
