    description: "Scharnhorst was a fast German capital ship armed with nine 28 cm guns and, by 1943, a heavy anti-aircraft battery. After commerce-raiding operations and the Norwegian campaign she moved to northern waters to threaten the Arctic convoys. In December 1943, at the Battle of the North Cape, HMS Duke of York and accompanying forces caught and sank her; only 36 of her crew survived.",
