    "description": "The Supermarine Walrus Mk I was a biplane amphibian flown by the Royal Navy's Fleet Air Arm and Commonwealth navies from 1935, catapult-launched from ships or operating from the water for fleet reconnaissance, gunnery spotting and air-sea rescue. Its pusher layout gave a maximum speed of about 217 km/h and a range of about 970 km; it was slow but famously sturdy and seaworthy. In game it is a scout with one .303-inch Vickers K gun in the bow and one behind the wings; its six 100 lb bombs or depth charges are not configured and are not listed in the reference.",
