    description: "The U.S. Navy's 18-inch/48-caliber Mark 1 was the largest-calibre naval gun ever designed for the service, a triple-turret weapon for 1920s capital ships. Only one prototype was built, and after the Washington Naval Treaty of 1922 banned guns above 16 inches it was relined as a 16-inch test gun and never entered service in its original form. In the game it serves as the main armament of the Lexington-class battlecruiser.",
