    description: "The J6K1 Jinpū was a land-based high-altitude interceptor designed for the Imperial Japanese Navy to counter the B-29. Developed from the J3K and powered by a 2,200 hp Homare 42, it was planned to carry two 30 mm Type 5 cannon and two 13.2 mm Type 3 machine guns. Only one unarmed prototype was completed before the programme was cancelled. In game it can carry two four-round 100 mm Type 3 rocket-bomb mounts, for eight anti-aircraft rockets.",
