    description: "The Hs 123 A-1 was Germany's first dive bomber and the Luftwaffe's last operational biplane, entering service in 1936. A BMW 132Dc radial of 880 PS drove a rugged airframe armed with two 7.92mm MG 17 machine guns and up to one 250 kg plus four 50 kg bombs. It gave close support in Spain and on the Eastern Front but went out of production in 1940.",
    author: "Unknown",
