    description: "The Hs 129 B-2 was a ground-attack aircraft adapted for anti-tank work on the Eastern Front, entering service in 1942. Its two 700 PS Gnome-Rhône 14M engines were underpowered, and it carried two 20mm MG 151/20 cannon and two 7.92mm MG 17 machine guns in the nose with six 50 kg bombs. The armoured «bathtub» cockpit had poor visibility, and its small numbers could not change the course of the fighting.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
