    ],
    description: "The Ar 234 B-2 was the world's first jet bomber to see combat, entering service in September 1944. Two Jumo 004B turbojets gave it a speed above 700 km/h that piston-engined fighters could barely match. It began as a high-speed reconnaissance aircraft; its fuel tanks filled the fuselage, so all 1,500 kg of bombs hung externally. Repeated attacks on the Remagen bridge in March 1945 were its best-known bombing missions.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
