    description: "The Do 17 E-1 was the earliest production bomber of the Do 17 family, entering service in 1937; its slender fuselage earned the nickname «Flying Pencil». Two 750 PS BMW VI 7.3D engines gave it a top speed of only about 330 km/h. A twin 7.92mm MG 15 on the dorsal position was its only defence, with ten 50 kg bombs internally and one 500 kg externally. It flew over Poland and France but was soon replaced.",
