    description: "The Ju 88 A-5 was the most numerous bomber variant of the Ju 88, reaching the front during the Battle of Britain in 1940. It was a transitional type, mating the old A-1 fuselage to the longer A-4 wing, and two Jumo 211 engines gave it speed, bomb load and versatility. Three 7.92mm MG 15 machine guns covered nose, dorsal and ventral positions, and two 500 kg with four 250 kg bombs fitted the bay.",
