    description: "The BV 138 C-1 was the German Navy's three-engined long-range maritime reconnaissance flying boat, entering service in March 1941. Boat hull and stub wings let it patrol the Atlantic and North Sea for long periods, hunting convoys and directing U-boats onto them, and its Jumo 205D diesels could be refuelled from submarines. Two 20mm MG 151/20, one 13mm MG 131 and two 7.92mm MG 15 defended it, with three 50 kg bombs under the wings; slow and lightly armed, it was easy prey.",
