    description: "The Fw 200 C-1 was converted from the Fw 200 long-range airliner and entered service in 1940, its four BMW 132 engines giving a range beyond 3,500 km. It hunted Allied shipping far out in the Atlantic, earning Churchill's name «scourge of the Atlantic», and sank the liner Empress of Britain in October 1940. Four 7.92mm MG 15 machine guns and four 250 kg bombs armed it, but its structure was weak and losses to escort fighters heavy.",
