    description: "The He 177 A-5 was the only German heavy bomber to reach mass production, built from December 1943. Two paired DB 610 engines each drove a four-bladed propeller, and poor cooling plus a dive-bombing requirement left it plagued by engine fires and the nickname «Reich's torch». Published figures give about 488 km/h and a range of 5,500-6,000 km; defensive armament ran from a 7.92mm MG 81 in the nose to 20mm MG 151/20 and 13mm MG 131 guns.",
