    description: "Vulkan was a submarine salvage and repair ship commissioned by the Imperial German Navy in 1908. Its catamaran hull allowed a 500-ton crane to lift a disabled submarine between the two hulls for transport and repair. Four boilers drove two turbo-generators and two propulsion motors, giving the 1,595-ton ship a maximum speed of 12 knots. After World War I she was handed over to Britain as reparations and sank during the voyage on 6 April 1919.",
