    description: "Norderney was a small German oil tanker commissioned in 1915 as W 84 and renamed Norderney later that year. She supplied fuel to Imperial German warships in coastal ports and anchorages. The 75.08 by 10.5 metre ship displaced about 2,864 tons, reached 10 knots and carried no armament. In 1920 she was converted into a cable ship, became the British prize Alert in 1945 and was scrapped in 1960.",
