    description: "Stuttgart was the third Königsberg-class light cruiser of the Imperial German Navy. In 1918 she was rebuilt as a fast seaplane tender: six 105 mm guns were removed, two 88 mm anti-aircraft guns were fitted forward, and two hangars for three seaplanes were installed aft. Without a catapult, each aircraft had to be lowered to the water for take-off and hoisted aboard after landing. Recommissioned in May 1918, she flew reconnaissance sorties in the German Bight and was surrendered to Britain in 1920.",
