    description: "Graf Zeppelin was the lead ship of Germany's Graf Zeppelin-class aircraft carriers. Launched in 1938, she was taken in hand again in 1942 for modification to the revised carrier-aircraft plan, but major work stopped after January 1943 and the ship never entered service. In its 1943 design state the carrier displaced about 33,550 long tons, measured 262.5 metres overall with a 36.2-metre beam, and had a designed speed of 33.8 knots. The original air group included Fi 167 torpedo bombers, while the 1942 revision replaced them with Bf 109 and Ju 87 aircraft.",
