    description: "The Fieseler Fi 167 was a biplane carrier torpedo bomber and reconnaissance aircraft developed for Graf Zeppelin. Its prototype first flew in 1938, and the pre-production aircraft combined strong low-speed control with short take-off and landing performance. Maximum level speed was about 325 km/h; armament comprised one forward-firing 7.92mm MG 17, one rear 7.92mm MG 15 and a single approximately 45cm aerial torpedo.",
