        label: "Torpedoes",
        value: "2x4 533mm",
      },
    ],
    description: "This is the destroyer design Ansaldo submitted to the Regia Marina in 1939. It was conceived to combine surface action with a strong anti-aircraft battery, and its main-battery turrets re-used the enclosed mount form of the contemporary 90 mm anti-aircraft gun, so the proposal is often read as an extension of the anti-aircraft destroyer idea. No order, name or builder was ever recorded; the artist reconstructed it from scattered data published at the time, and the design remained on paper. The proposal left no ship name; following the Regia Marina's custom of naming destroyers after winds, this entry calls it Tramontana, the north wind.",
    author: "Tzoli",
    links: [
