        label: "Torpedoes",
        value: "2x3 533mm",
      },
    ],
    description: "Folgore was the lead ship of the four-destroyer Folgore class, generally treated as the second series of the Freccia (Dardo) class. Commissioned in 1932 she served with Fulmine, Lampo and Baleno in the VIII Torpedo Destroyer Flotilla, the four sharing the motto Folgor in hostem — lightning upon the enemy. She sailed from Taranto in July 1940 to cover the convoy to Libya and took part in the Battle of Punta Stilo; a 1941 refit removed all of the original machine guns. The artwork combines the side and top views and follows the pre-war Regia Marina scheme used in 1940.",
    author: "Sam#28",
