    description: "Dardo was one of the four Freccia (Dardo) class destroyers, commissioned in January 1932 and serving with Freccia, Saetta and Strale in the VII Torpedo Destroyer Flotilla. Through the war she escorted Mediterranean convoys to Libya; after the September 1943 armistice Germany took her over as TA31, and she was lost in April 1945. The artwork combines the side and top views, was drawn by Jerzy Lewandowski and is marked as representing her in 1940.",
