        value: "2x IMAM Ro.43",
      },
    ],
    description: "Project UP-102 is the big-gun cruiser Ansaldo offered to Romania in 1937. Its concept follows the German Panzerschiffe: a small number of heavy guns for long-range engagement, with a dual-purpose secondary battery of one calibre replacing the mixed 15 cm and 10.5 cm guns of the German ships. Enclosed 40 mm Bofors mounts were worked in beside the main turrets so that loading would not be disrupted by the blast of the main battery. The offer was aimed at the export market and was never ordered; the drawing shows both the Italian and Romanian versions, and this entry follows the Italian-flagged one. The artist's second German floatplane on the Romanian version is represented here by a second Italian aircraft of the same role. The project itself carried no ship name; following the Italian custom of naming heavy cruisers after cities, this entry uses Venezia.",
    author: "Tzoli",
    links: [
