        label: "Aerial Torpedo",
        value: "1 x 400mm Type 1926 DA",
      },
    ],
    description: "The Latécoère 298 was a single-engine twin-float torpedo seaplane introduced by the French Navy in 1938, also used for dive bombing and maritime reconnaissance. Powered by an 880 hp Hispano-Suiza 12Ycrs, it had a maximum speed of about 295 km/h. Two fixed forward-firing 7.5mm Darne machine guns were mounted in the wings and a third served as a flexible rear gun; the ventral crutch carried one 400mm Type 1926 DA aerial torpedo. It operated from French coastal bases and the seaplane tender Commandant Teste, becoming one of the French Navy's most successful wartime seaplanes.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
      {
        name: "Wikipedia - Latécoère 298",
        url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lat%C3%A9co%C3%A8re_298",
      },
    ],
