        value: "1 x 400mm Model 1926 DA",
      },
    ],
    description: "The Bréguet Br.810 was a twin-engine carrier torpedo bomber selected by the French Navy in 1939 for the Joffre-class carriers. Derived from the Br.693 attack aircraft, it added an arrestor hook, dive brakes and folding wings for level bombing, torpedo attacks and long-range scouting. The prototype was not completed before the 1940 armistice. Game performance is approximated from the Br.693 and adjusted for carrier equipment and torpedo carriage.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
