      {
        label: "Machine Gun (Rear Cockpit)",
        value: "1 x 7.5mm Darne",
      },
    ],
    description: "The Loire 130 was a single-engine high-wing reconnaissance flying boat introduced by the French Navy in 1937 and operated from battleships, cruisers and the seaplane tender Commandant Teste. Its Hispano-Suiza liquid-cooled V12 gave a maximum speed of about 245 km/h and a range of about 1,100 km, supporting fleet reconnaissance, observation and liaison duties. The game has no dedicated reconnaissance behaviour, so it is represented as an other-type aircraft; its reference data retains one fixed forward and one rear flexible 7.5mm Darne machine gun.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
      {
        name: "Wikipedia - Loire 130",
        url: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loire_130",
      },
    ],
