      {
        label: "Bomb (Dive Bombing)",
        value: "2 x 225kg",
      },
    ],
    description: "The Vought V-156F was the French Navy export version of the SB2U Vindicator, beginning delivery in 1939. It served with the AB 1 and AB 3 escadrilles of the carrier Béarn and later from shore bases on maritime patrol, anti-submarine and strike duties. An 825 hp Pratt & Whitney R-1535 gave a sea-level maximum speed of about 375 km/h and the aircraft had a range of about 1,169 km. The French version used French radio equipment, 7.5mm Darne guns and wing fence-type dive brakes. Because the centreline bomb displacement gear was not installed as planned, most combat missions relied on underwing racks; the aircraft is represented as a dive bomber in game.",
    author: "Unknown",
    links: [
