      }
    ],
    "description": "The Fiat CR.42 Falco was a single-seat biplane fighter that entered service with the Italian Air Force in 1939. Built on a steel-tube frame with fabric covering, it was Italy's frontline fighter at the start of the war and one of the last biplane fighters produced in large numbers. Maximum speed was about 441 km/h with a range of 780 km. In game it is a fighter armed with two forward-firing 12.7 mm Breda-SAFAT machine guns; no bombs are configured.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
      {
        "name": "Wikipedia - Fiat_CR.42",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fiat_CR.42"
      }
    ]
  },
