    ],
    "description": "The Macchi C.200 Saetta was a single-seat monoplane fighter that entered service in 1939. Its radial engine and robust airframe gave it excellent handling, and it supported the Italian fighter force early in the war. Maximum speed was about 504 km/h with a range of 570 km. In game it is a fighter armed with two forward-firing 12.7 mm Breda-SAFAT machine guns; no bombs are configured.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
