      }
    ],
    "description": "The Macchi C.202 Folgore was the liquid-cooled development of the C.200, entering service in 1941 with an Alfa Romeo-built DB 601 engine. Far faster than its predecessor, it became Italy's principal fighter through 1942-43. Maximum speed was about 600 km/h with a range of 765 km. In game it is a fighter armed with two 12.7 mm nose machine guns and two 7.7 mm wing guns; no bombs are configured.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
      {
