    ],
    "description": "The Cant Z.1007bis Alcione was a three-engined medium bomber that entered service in 1939, notable for its wooden airframe. Together with the SM.79 and BR.20 it formed Italy's medium bomber force early in the war. Maximum speed was about 458 km/h with a range of 1,795 km. In game it is a level bomber armed with one forward 7.7 mm gun, dorsal and ventral 12.7 mm guns, one waist gun and four 500 kg bombs.",
