        "value": "2 x 450mm"
      }
    ],
    "description": "The Savoia-Marchetti SM.79bis Sparviero developed from the three-engined medium bomber that entered service in 1936; the SM.79-III torpedo variant, also known as bis, joined anti-shipping service in late 1942 and became the backbone of Italy's torpedo bombers. Maximum speed was about 460 km/h with a range of 2,600 km. In game it is a torpedo bomber armed with 12.7 mm nose and dorsal guns, two 7.7 mm waist guns and two 450 mm torpedoes; no bombs are configured.",
