    "description": "The IMAM Ro.37bis Lince was a two-seat biplane used by Italian army aviation in the mid-1930s for battlefield reconnaissance and liaison work. Maximum speed was about 330 km/h with a range of 1,120 km. In game it is a scout armed with two forward 7.7 mm guns and one rear-cockpit gun; no bombs are configured.",
