      }
    ],
    "description": "The IMAM Ro.43 was a catapult-launched shipboard reconnaissance floatplane that entered Italian naval service in 1935, flown from cruisers and battleships for long-range scouting on a central main float with wingtip floats. Maximum speed was about 300 km/h with a range of 800-1,500 km. In game it is a scout armed with one forward and one rear-cockpit 7.7 mm gun; no bombs are configured.",
