  {
    "name": "MiG-1",
    "displayName": "MiG-1",
    "type": "Fighter",
    "armaments": [
      {
        "label": "Nose (12.7mm UBS, synchronized)",
        "value": "1 x 12.7mm UBS",
      },
      {
        "label": "Nose (2 x 7.62mm ShKAS, synchronized)",
        "value": "2 x 7.62mm ShKAS",
      }
    ],
    "description": "The Mikoyan-Gurevich MiG-1 (I-200) was a high-altitude interceptor that entered production in 1940. Powered by an AM-35A, it reached about 636 km/h at altitude but handled poorly at low level and had a range of only some 580 km. Armament was one synchronized 12.7mm UBS and two 7.62mm ShKAS machine guns in the nose. In game it is treated as a fighter armed only with its synchronized nose machine guns; bomb racks are not configured and are not listed here.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
      {
        "name": "Wikipedia — MiG-1",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikoyan-Gurevich_MiG-1",
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "MiG-3",
    "displayName": "MiG-3",
    "type": "Fighter",
    "armaments": [
      {
        "label": "Nose (12.7mm UBS, synchronized)",
        "value": "1 x 12.7mm UBS",
      },
      {
        "label": "Nose (2 x 7.62mm ShKAS, synchronized)",
        "value": "2 x 7.62mm ShKAS",
      }
    ],
    "description": "The MiG-3 was the improved production development of the MiG-1, entering service in 1941. It was likewise optimized for altitude and clumsy at low level, with a maximum speed of 640 km/h, a range of about 820 km, a length of 8.25 m and a span of 10.20 m. Armament matched the MiG-1: one synchronized 12.7mm UBS and two 7.62mm ShKAS in the nose. In game it is treated as a fighter armed only with its synchronized nose machine guns; bomb racks are not configured and are not listed here.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
      {
        "name": "Wikipedia — MiG-3",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikoyan-Gurevich_MiG-3",
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "La-5",
    "displayName": "La-5",
    "type": "Fighter",
    "armaments": [
      {
        "label": "Nose Cowl (2 x 20mm ShVAK, synchronized)",
        "value": "2 x 20mm ShVAK",
      }
    ],
    "description": "The La-5 was Lavochkin's 1942 re-engining of the LaGG-3 with the M-82 radial, which markedly improved climb and turning performance at low level; maximum speed was about 580 km/h. For this game the range is conservatively taken as the La-5FN's 765 km. Armament was two 20mm ShVAK cannon in the nose cowl. In game it is treated as a fighter with twin nose cannon; bomb racks are not configured and are not listed here.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
      {
        "name": "Wikipedia — La-5",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavochkin_La-5",
      },
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "La-7",
    "displayName": "La-7",
    "type": "Fighter",
    "armaments": [
      {
        "label": "Nose Cowl (3 x 20mm B-20)",
        "value": "3 x 20mm B-20",
      }
    ],
    "description": "The La-7 was a thorough refinement of the La-5 that entered service in 1944. With a maximum speed of 661 km/h it was one of the best low-altitude piston fighters of the war. From January 1945 it was fitted with three 20mm B-20 cannon, which is the armament configured here. In game it is treated as a fighter; bomb racks are not configured and are not listed here.",
    "author": "Unknown",
    "links": [
      {
        "name": "Wikipedia — La-7",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavochkin_La-7",
      },
    ]
