    description: "Littorio was the lead ship of the Vittorio Veneto class, laid down in October 1934 and commissioned in May 1940 as Italy's answer to the French Dunkerque class. She was the first Italian battleship with the Pugliese underwater protection system and carried a 350 mm midships belt. Torpedoed and beached at Taranto in November 1940, she rejoined the fleet in March 1941, was renamed Italia in July 1943, sailed to Malta under the armistice, and was scrapped in 1948.",
