      {
        label: "Reconnaissance Seaplanes",
        value: "1x IMAM Ro.43",
      },
    ],
    description: "Caio Duilio belonged to the Andrea Doria class, also called the Caio Duilio class, both laid down before the First World War. Between 1937 and 1940 she was rebuilt at Genoa: the amidships turret was removed, boilers and machinery were replaced, the bridge was redesigned and horizontal protection and underwater defence were strengthened, which made her fast enough to operate with the new battleships. She served in the First Battleship Division on convoy and fleet sorties, lay idle after 1942 for lack of fuel, and was scrapped in 1956.",
    author: "voodoo",
    links: [
      {
        name: "voodoo-world.cz - Caio Duilio class",
        url: "https://www.voodoo-world.cz/battleships/italy/doria.html",
