        value: "6x2 37mm/54 Breda",
      },
      {
        label: "Reconnaissance Seaplanes",
        value: "1x IMAM Ro.43",
      },
    ],
    description: "Giulio Cesare was the second ship of the Conte di Cavour class and served from the First World War. Rebuilt at Genoa between 1933 and 1937 along the same lines as the Andrea Doria class, she gained speed and a far stronger anti-aircraft battery. On 9 July 1940, during the action off Punta Stilo, she was hit at about 24,000 metres by the British battleship Warspite, one of the best known long-range hits on a moving target. She spent the rest of the war on convoy and diversion duties, was struck from the list in 1948 and handed to the Soviet Union as war reparations.",
    author: "voodoo",
    links: [
      {
        name: "voodoo-world.cz - Conte di Cavour class",
